 "about": "CoffeeRecs starter catalog (2026-10-24): current home espresso machines, grinders, brewers (pour-over drippers, immersion brewers and drip coffee makers), kettles and scales. Every value was read on 2026-10-24 from the page linked in sources: the maker's own page where it can be read (Fellow, Acaia, Timemore, Hario, AeroPress, Comandante, Weber Workshops, Chemex, Kalita, Ratio, Moccamaster, Varia, Wacaco, Turin, Gaggia, Flair, Breville, Baratza, Niche, 1Zpresso, Decent, Cafelat), otherwise the US retailer Whole Latte Love's product page (Rancilio, Lelit, Profitec, ECM, Rocket Espresso, De'Longhi, Eureka, Mahlkönig, Brewista, Bonavita), whose maker sites could not be read; Turin DF54 comes from DF Grinders' page. Anything not stated there is blank. One entry per model as the maker names it; sizes and materials sold under one model name are one entry (Hario V60 01/02/03 in ceramic, plastic, glass or metal; Kalita Wave 155 or 185 in glass or steel; Chemex Classic 3 to 10 cup), but a different model, generation or version is not (Breville Barista Express vs Barista Express Impress, Baratza Encore vs Encore ESP vs Encore ESP Pro, Profitec GO vs GO 2.0, Lelit Mara X vs Mara X3, Timemore C3 vs C3s, Fellow Opus 2, Ode Gen 2). Columns: shape = category, balance = type, surface = key specs (burrs, boiler, portafilter, capacity), core = main material, weight = weight as the page states it. No model years. Added 2026-10-25 from reviews held as missing products: La Marzocco Linea Micra (maker page), Timemore Sculptor 064S (the first-generation 064S, maker's Sculptor series page), Eureka Mignon Specialita and the first Fellow Opus (Whole Latte Love pages).",
